+## THE LODE PLANE: cell (Vector2i) -> vein material id (&"ore", &"coal", &"iron", &"rich_ore"). Sparse.
+##
+## This is where ore is BORN, and the cell it names is still solid host rock in `blocks` — the two grids
+## describe the same cell answering two different questions. `blocks` says *what you carve*; `lodes` says
+## *what is in there*. A generator that writes a lode without leaving rock in front of it has not made a
+## vein, it has made a hole with ore lying in it.
+##
+## Before the cutover (`docs/LODE_PLAN.md` phase 3) a vein was an ore BLOCK: a cell whose foreground
+## material was &"ore", which meant that clearing the rock and taking the ore were the same act, and every
+## blow that widened a tunnel through a vein silently destroyed the rest of it. Moving ore to its own plane
+## is what makes the two acts separable, and it is the whole point of the migration.
+##
+## Richness for a lode cell lives in `amounts`, exactly as it did when the vein was a block — which is why
+## the cutover left the richness pipeline (depth-scaling, drought, the aquifer's rich roll) untouched.
+var lodes: Dictionary = {}
